-# Docker completion acceptance experiment
-
-This workspace implements the exact 24-execution parent-exit experiment in
-`experiment.py`. Six deterministic adversarial fixtures and six matched clean
-controls run serially in primary and replay phases. A 20 ms `/proc` observer
-computes both the naive and PID-reuse-safe process-tree-aware decisions from the
-same sample stream.
+# Docker parent-exit completion experiment
 
-The runner captures the active daemon endpoint before creating files, uses a
-fresh experiment-owned Docker configuration for every later Docker command,
-only reads existing plugin directories, never pulls or builds an image, and
-does not mutate any pre-existing Docker configuration or CLI plugin.
+`experiment.py` is the Python 3.12, standard-library-only host harness. It
+strictly uses `DOCKER_HOST=unix:///var/run/docker.sock`, runs three independent
+Docker gates, resolves a preloaded Linux Python 3.12 image to an immutable ID,
+builds the fixture with `--network=none`, and runs a smoke container before the
+timed section.
 
-## Run
+When preflight passes, it sequentially runs the fixed order
+`D1,C1,...,D6,C6` and then the identical replay order. The fixture image runs
+`fixture/monitor.py` as PID 1. That process creates each requested topology and
+observes parent exit, retained PID/starttime descendant identities, and declared
+output descriptors at a 10 ms cadence.
 
-Preload `python:3.12-alpine` as a Linux/arm64 image first, or set
